🔹 JavaScript (Most Important Round)
1. What is Closure?

Answer (interview-ready):
A closure is when a function remembers variables from its lexical scope even after the outer function has finished execution.

Example:

function outer() {
  let count = 0;
  return function inner() {
    count++;
    return count;
  };
}

const fn = outer();
console.log(fn()); // 1
console.log(fn()); // 2

Where used:

Data hiding (private variables)
Currying
Debounce/throttle
React hooks internally
