3. Debounce vs Throttle
Debounce

Executes after delay (last call only)

function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}
Throttle

Executes at fixed intervals

function throttle(fn, limit) {
  let flag = true;
  return function (...args) {
    if (!flag) return;
    fn.apply(this, args);
    flag = false;
    setTimeout(() => flag = true, limit);
  };
}
4. How "this" Works
Context	Value of this
Global	window (browser)
Function	window / undefined (strict mode)
Object method	object itself
Arrow function	inherits from parent
Constructor	new object

Example:

const obj = {
  name: "Vedant",
  normal: function() { console.log(this.name); },
  arrow: () => console.log(this.name)
};

obj.normal(); // Vedant
obj.arrow();  // undefined
5. Promise vs Async/Await
Feature	Promise	Async/Await
Syntax	.then()	cleaner
Readability	harder	easier
Error Handling	.catch()	try/catch

Example:

async function fetchData() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url);
    const data = await res.json();
    return data;
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
  }
}
