2. useMemo vs useCallback vs React.memo
Tool	Purpose
useMemo	Memoize value
useCallback	Memoize function
React.memo	Prevent component re-render

Example:

const memoizedValue = useMemo(() => compute(), [dep]);
const memoizedFn = useCallback(() => {}, [dep]);

export default React.memo(Component);
3. useEffect Lifecycle

Runs after render.

useEffect(() => {
  // mount + update
  return () => {
    // cleanup (unmount)
  };
}, [dependencies]);

Cases:

[] → runs once
[dep] → runs when dep changes
no deps → runs every render
